{"step_index":84,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:16:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T23:46:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T23:46:46+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 204\nTotal Bytes: 7106\nShowing lines 1 to 204\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: find-skills\n3: description: Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Find Skills (Windows Compatible Version)\n7: \n8: This skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n9: \n10: **This is a Windows-compatible fork that fixes the empty output issue in Claude Code on Windows.**\n11: \n12: ## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Windows Compatibility\n13: \n14: **On Windows, you MUST use PowerShell to run skills commands!**\n15: \n16: The default Bash/Git Bash environment on Windows does NOT work with `npx skills` - commands will return empty output.\n17: \n18: **Always use this format on Windows:**\n19: ```bash\n20: powershell -Command \"npx skills find '[query]'\"\n21: powershell -Command \"npx skills add [package] -g -y\"\n22: powershell -Command \"npx skills list -g\"\n23: ```\n24: \n25: **Example:**\n26: ```bash\n27: # ❌ WRONG - will return empty on Windows\n28: npx skills find \"react\"\n29: \n30: # ✅ CORRECT - works on Windows\n31: powershell -Command \"npx skills find 'react'\"\n32: ```\n33: \n34: ## When to Use This Skill\n35: \n36: Use this skill when the user:\n37: \n38: - Asks